UPDATE "citation_mining" SET "notes" = '[backward 2026-09-20 03:04] PASS RAN, EXECUTED AGAINST THE PRINTED BIBLIOGRAPHY RATHER THAN AN API, AND YIELDED ONE NEW CANDIDATE. Assigned by batch 18 section 9 item 1; the deferral it discharges was a depth-1 design deferral, not capacity. NO CROSSREF DEPOSIT EXISTS for this report, so there was no reference list to fetch: the 38 entries were transcribed from the persisted ED184280 PDF at pypdf page indices 167-169 and persisted as a DERIVED artefact (retrieval-log/<session>/08263082ebdda8eb.json), which is marked derived rather than retrieved because nobody served it. DERIVE THE YIELD, NEVER QUOTE IT: python3 scripts/research/mining_screen.py --ref REF-01005 --compare. It reports a BAND -- floor scores a reading that substitutes no letters, ceiling a best reading of damaged OCR -- and mining_screen.py was extended this batch to do that, because scoring a transcription as though it were a publisher deposit is the error this whole screen registry exists to stop. NEW CANDIDATE: 116 (Corlett et al., Applied Ergonomics 3, ramps-versus-stairs, title partly reconstructed). ALREADY STAGED AND NOW ENRICHED: 110 (Elmer) gains an author, a form and a body-text date; 115 (Templer) is corrected, see below; 109 (Walter) gains corroboration for its 1971 year from footnote c. THE PASS''S MOST USEFUL RESULT IS A NEGATIVE ONE: Walter''s entry does not score under any screen, because its title in this bibliography carries no slope term -- ''Part 3: Ramp gradients'' is a part title. The single most slope-relevant item in the list is invisible to a title screen, which bounds what any yield on this anchor can mean. SATURATED: the list runs alphabetically ANSI to Webb with no break, so it is complete rather than truncated, and there is no second reference list in this document to mine.

DEFERRAL DISCHARGED 2026-09-20 03:04 by session_2026-09-20-research-batch-19-pre1990-chain-steinfeld-walter-templer (backward pass). It read: DEPTH-1 DEFERRAL (citation-miner section 6), design rather than capacity: REF-01005 was admitted THIS batch, so mining it here would be depth-2 in one pass. Legitimate under the owner ruling of 2026-09-18 ("deferred is okay so long as it runs eventually"), and ASSIGNED rather than left to age — THE NEXT BATCH TAKES IT AND IT IS THE HIGHEST-VALUE BACKWARD TARGET ON THIS SLUG. Reason: Table 13 footnote c names Templer 1977 and Walter 1971 as the warrants for its recommendation table, and the Comparison section names Elmer 1957, so its reference list is the index to the entire pre-1990 ramp-gradient layer GAP-028 identified as structurally unreachable — held by a document this project now has in full. NOTE THE RETRIEVAL ASYMMETRY, because it changes what a mining pass means here: no Crossref deposit exists, so there is NO machine-readable reference list. The pass runs against the PDF bibliography (page indices 167 onward, OCR damaged), not against an API, and a yield from it must name a screen from governance/mining-screens.yaml and be derived by scripts/research/mining_screen.py per the owner rule of 2026-09-18 22:55.', "updated_at" = '2026-09-20 03:04', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-09-20-research-batch-19-pre1990-chain-steinfeld-walter-templer', "deferred_reason" = NULL WHERE "slug" = 'accessible-circulation-geometry' AND "local_ref_id" = 'RAMP-HIST-01';

